<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edmund Barton</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1849">1849</a>–<a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edmund Barton was an Australian lawyer and politician who led the federation movement in the 1890s. He became the first prime minister of the Commonwealth of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> in 1901, when Parliament met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/melbourne">Melbourne</a>, and his government passed the Immigration Restriction Act. In 1903 he left office to become a founding justice of the High Court.</p></div>
